<title>ITALY: Italy's Prodi to meet Kohl in Bonn on February 7.</title>
<headline>Italy's Prodi to meet Kohl in Bonn on February 7.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy and Germany will hold a bilateral summit in Bonn on February 7, diplomatic sources said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The talks will bring together Italian Prime Minister Romano Prodi and Chancellor Helmut Kohl as well as their key ministers.</p>
<p>The meeting will follow bilateral talks between Prodi and British Prime Minister John Major in London on January 31 which were announced on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Officials have given no details of the talks.</p>
<p>Diplomatic sources say the main themes are certain to include Europe's planned economic and monetary union and reforms to the European Union's workings and institutions.</p>
</text>
